With the vault inside the repo, `--tier project` (the default) creates `{vault}/specs/` and its
README, prints one line per action, then the tier root.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
vault_path: ./vault
latest_migration: 9999
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/sprints.md --
sprints
-- cmd --
booping specs init
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
created dir {CWD}/vault/specs
created file {CWD}/vault/specs/README.md
{CWD}/vault/specs
-- stderr --
-- expected/cwd/vault/specs/README.md --
# specs/

This project's specs tier: values, rules, ADRs and the other typed records, in booping's specs format — the guide is `src/specs/README.md` in the booping plugin. Check with `booping specs check --tier project`.
